---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="How Simply Plant Care researches, checks, and updates its guides — and how corrections work."
  canonicalPath="/editorial-policy/"
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">Editorial Policy</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
  <p class="article-meta">Last updated: 26 November 2026</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Who writes and reviews the guides</h2>
    <p>
      Every guide on Simply Plant Care is written and reviewed by
      <a href="/author/zeeshan-farooq/">Zeeshan Farooq</a>, a plants
      researcher. He is the site's only author. No guide is published
      under a made-up author name, and no credentials are claimed that he
      does not hold.
    </p>
    <h2>What we publish</h2>
    <p>
      We publish practical indoor plant care guides and free tools. Every
      guide answers a specific question a plant owner would actually ask —
      how to water a particular plant, what light it needs, or what to do
      about a specific problem.
    </p>
    <h2>How guides are researched</h2>
    <p>
      Guides are written by Zeeshan Farooq from general horticultural
      knowledge and checked against public references, including university
      extension services and botanical gardens. We do not copy content from
      other websites. Where a topic is genuinely debated — for example,
      whether misting raises humidity meaningfully — we say so instead of
      presenting one view as settled fact. Each guide covers one specific
      question: a full care routine, watering only, light only, or the
      first month for a beginner. Related guides link to each other and
      state what they cover, so readers — and search engines — can tell
      them apart.
    </p>
    <h2>Fact-checking</h2>
    <p>
      Before publication, each guide is reviewed for clear errors: wrong
      plant names, watering advice that contradicts the plant's needs, and
      claims that do not match the references. We do not invent statistics,
      studies, or quotes. If a guide cites a source type (such as a
      university extension service), it is named as a source type, not as a
      fabricated specific claim.
    </p>
    <h2>Updates</h2>
    <p>
      Guides are reviewed and updated when new information comes to light
      or when readers point out a problem. Each guide shows its publication
      and last-updated dates.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If you spot an error, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> with
      the guide name and what is wrong. We correct factual errors promptly
      and note the update date on the guide.
    </p>
    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not publish paid or sponsored guides.</li>
      <li>We do not accept payment to recommend a product.</li>
      <li>We do not invent author credentials, testimonials, or reviews.</li>
      <li>We do not present the Plant Problem Solver's suggestions as a diagnosis.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      The site may display advertising in the future. Advertising, if
      added, will be clearly separate from editorial content, and it will
      not influence what our guides recommend.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
